sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch09-02> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch09-02--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch09-02--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch09-02: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.56" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.56"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.58"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Rods, arms and survival are an obvious confirming and refuting pattern, and the contrast with seawater controls is discriminating. The observations exist in the experimental literature, including later repeats of calcium-free culture, but they are not gathered in a public dataset that can be reanalysed as data. A literature compilation can test the claim for the species that were reared and cannot underwrite the broader extension." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: In published lime-free versus normal seawater rearings of echinoid embryos, score skeletal-rod presence, larval-arm length and survival. Suppression of rods and arms with continued development supports the claim; normal skeletons, or death rather than skeleton-less development, refutes it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The rearings are reported as figures in papers, not as a reusable open table of larvae, treatments and phenotypes.", "Apparently healthy is loosely defined, and the published experiments cover a few echinoid species rather than skeleton-forming organisms generally." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch09-02--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch09-02 by Grok 4.7: 0.85" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.85"^^xsd:double ;
